  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reactor - Women Safety in Action: Building Gender Inclusive Public Spaces</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Within the Kvinnna till Kvinna Foundation&#x2019;s regional programme &quot;Democracy and Resilience in the Western Balkans: Supporting Feminist Change Agents&quot; the partner organisation Reactor is implementing the 12-month programme &quot;Women Safety in Action: Building Gender Inclusive Public Spaces&quot;. The project focuses on comprehensive research on safety (GBV/VAWG) in public spaces, evidence-based advocacy and engaging media in reporting on GBV/ VAWG in public spaces. In the project Reactor will directly partner with the media oriented CSO &#x2018;Ladybug&#x2019; that focus on gender-sensitive media reporting and addresses audiences of Albanian ethnicity.</narrative>
  </description>
